  "cues": [
   [
    0.104,
    "A catalyst is a chemical agent that speeds up a reaction without being consumed by it."
   ],
   [
    5.573,
    "An enzyme is a catalytic protein."
   ],
   [
    8.06,
    "Take sucrose, table sugar: a glucose and a fructose joined together."
   ],
   [
    13.425,
    "With water, it can be split apart."
   ],
   [
    15.664,
    "This is hydrolysis, and the enzyme sucrase carries it out."
   ],
   [
    19.831,
    "The bond between the two sugars breaks, water divides into H and O H, and one piece goes to each sugar."
   ],
   [
    27.5,
    "And sucrase comes out unchanged, ready for the next sucrose."
   ],
   [
    31.654,
    "One enzyme molecule can do this again and again, which is why a cell needs only a little of it."
   ],
   [
    37.878,
    "Notice that sucrase is a protein, and it works on sucrose only."
   ],
   [
    42.409,
    "Every step of our pathway has its own enzyme."
   ]
  ]
