  "cues": [
   [
    0.104,
    "Every reaction between molecules involves breaking old bonds and forming new ones."
   ],
   [
    5.833,
    "Draw it as a curve, with free energy going up, and the progress of the reaction going across."
   ],
   [
    11.966,
    "The reactants sit on the left."
   ],
   [
    13.919,
    "The products sit lower, on the right, so delta G is negative, and the reaction is downhill."
   ],
   [
    20.326,
    "But between them stands a hill."
   ],
   [
    22.109,
    "To get over it, the molecules must first strain their bonds into an unstable transition state."
   ],
   [
    28.451,
    "The energy needed to climb that hill is the free energy of activation, or simply, the activation energy."
   ],
   [
    35.547,
    "Think of a ball resting in a dip, behind a ridge."
   ],
   [
    38.841,
    "Beyond the ridge it rolls downhill, but first it needs a push."
   ],
   [
    42.682,
    "A reaction can be downhill overall, and still be stuck at the bottom of that dip."
   ],
   [
    47.591,
    "That is why a downhill reaction is not always a fast one."
   ]
  ]
 },
